{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066711-2e-pack-concepts","id":1066711,"title":"[2E] Pack concepts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-22T22:57:55-07:00","id":1066711,"title":"[2E] Pack concepts","content":"In near future I plan to run 2E game and will need players to choose base concept of their Pack. As it will probably be newbies, I want to ease them this by preparing list of possible Packs concepts. So please, write your own. And if you are in mood, you can expend those ideas with proper example of particular Pack and it's Hunts. I will extend list by your ideas. List started by supplement <b>The Pack</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Packs concepts:</b><ul><li>AA or other support group</li> <li>Bikers club</li> <li>Band of musicians</li> <li>Clinic, health</li> <li>College fraternity or sorority</li> <li>Dojo of martial arts</li> <li>Detective agency</li> <li>Dysfunctional family</li> <li>Firefighters department</li> <li>Freemasons</li> <li>Gang</li> <li>Indie games developers studio</li> <li>Junta of a Tropico style island banana republic</li> <li>Library employees</li> <li>Mafia family</li> <li>Military unit</li> <li>Monastery</li> <li>Movie/television studio</li> <li>Neighborhood watch</li> <li>Nomadic Pack, doing tours on wide terrain</li> <li>\u2018Old faith\u2019 ( pagan ) cult</li> <li>\u2018Old money\u2019 family</li> <li>Park Ranger patrol</li> <li>Police unit</li> <li>Political party</li> <li>Pyramid scheme founders, Multi Level Marketing</li> <li>Reality prank show crew</li> <li>Regional historical society</li> <li>Secret Shoppers</li> <li>School for Gifted Youngsters</li> <li>Summer camp, staff and counselors</li> <li>Surgical team</li> <li>Terrorist cell</li> <li>Trade union</li> <li>Think tank researchers</li> <li>Tiger team hackers</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-26-2017, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T00:33:18-07:00","id":1066724,"title":"","content":"Many a moon ago (no pun intended) I ran a one shot at a con where the Packs were all based off the Warriors. If you want I could try and dig out my notes and share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 03-23-2017, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T02:08:11-07:00","id":1066744,"title":"","content":"My game's pack is based off a detective agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T05:10:08-07:00","id":1066783,"title":"","content":"Hunters in Darkness(/Iron Masters) pack as a Park Ranger patrol would work well<br /> <br /> They'd have to leave and come back under different identities pretty frequently to avoid being scrutinized for their seeming agelessness unless they have Hunter or supernatural friends in government who can deflect records checks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 03-23-2017, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:58:41-07:00","id":1067118,"title":"","content":"Band of musicians (mostly iron masters and blood talons, maybe some bone shadows)<br /> <br /> Nomadic Pack that uses their tours as cover for nation wide hunts<br /> <br /> Movie/television studio (Iron Masters Bone Shadows and Storm Lords)<br /> <br /> Pack that uses human mass media to influence the shadow.<br /> <br /> Junta of a Tropico style island banana republic (One high primal urge werewolf of each tribe and auspice)<br /> <br /> You know you want to...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:26:28-07:00","id":1067175,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for a pack based out of a summer camp. The staff and counselors are mostly Wolf-Blooded and humans (<i>probably</i> don't want twitchy werewolves dealing with large groups of children) who use their access to screen the campers for unaware Wolf-Blooded and those with the potential for First Change. The core of Uratha might be park rangers or other support staff, who have an excuse to wander around but don't need to actually deal with the public. Their territory would probably include the camp itself and maybe the nearby town(s) and countryside. (rural, obviously)<br /> <br /> The best thing is, if any group has a socially acceptable excuse for weird rituals and odd personalities, it's a scouting organization. ;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:55:06-07:00","id":1067191,"title":"","content":"Playing off the X-Men angle I've suggested before: A School for Gifted Youngsters<br /> <br /> Also similar to the Summer Camp idea above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:15:16-07:00","id":1067200,"title":"","content":"The recent death of Kim Jong-un's half brother makes me realize that a reality prank show crew could be a decent cover for a traveling pack and their hunts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:22:55-07:00","id":1067205,"title":"","content":"In that vein, a news crew.<br /> <br /> A political party. A tiger team. A think tank. Martial arts dojo. College fraternity or sorority. AA or other support group. Pyramid scheme founders. Trade union. Terrorist cell. Library employees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T19:18:11-07:00","id":1067312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066711-2e-pack-concepts?p=1067205#post1067205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that vein, a news crew.<br /> <br /> A political party. A tiger team. A think tank. Martial arts dojo. College fraternity or sorority. AA or other support group. Pyramid scheme founders. Trade union. Terrorist cell. Library employees.</div> </div> </div> </div>I 2nd the pyramid scheme one. Here in the US, in case Wyrd is unaware of one America's weirder political issues, there is a type of legal pyramid scheme called an Multi Level Marketing or MLM scheme that often has elements of cult behavior among their members and founders (fun fact:Trump's education is from a family that founded the Amway MLM and it is definitly a <a href=\"http://mycultlife.com/cults-3/why-amway-is-a-cult/\" target=\"_blank\">cult</a>.)<br /> <br /> You could totally have a pack that runs a creepy cultish MLM, though they will probably become Bale Hounds at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T19:20:55-07:00","id":1067313,"title":"","content":"COBRA, of GI-Joe fame, sort of started as a pyramid scheme and I've always pondered about turning it into a lodge or mot of some sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T00:49:54-07:00","id":1067940,"title":"","content":"A dysfunctional family, whose mysterious matriarch lives at the edge of a tiny little Deep South town. The blood of the wolf runs strong, and any scions who show it are...brought home, whether they like it or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T00:53:00-07:00","id":1067942,"title":"","content":"A neighborhood watch. Everyone knows they want the best for the town / neighborhood / city, but they're a little...intense for a lot of people. There's a small core of diehards - they patrol every night, cleaning graffiti and chasing off anyone who loiters too long - but practically everyone in town is sympathetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T00:55:38-07:00","id":1067943,"title":"","content":"The Secret Shoppers. A young pack based in a shopping center. It's like a city in miniature, and although the Gauntlet is strong the Essence is plentifu. Other packs have always overlooked its importance, but hat just leaves more territory for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:41:55-07:00","id":1067976,"title":"","content":"A surgical team composed of a core of nurses and doctors with an incredible success rate and are the current poster kids for the Hospital's campaign on teamwork. Of course, they don't work well with others, and the few times there's had to be a float in their OR, the atmosphere was incredibly tense.<br /> <br /> They work insane hours too. Eesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T21:24:55-07:00","id":1068171,"title":"","content":"Nice, Aynie!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T22:33:56-07:00","id":1068186,"title":"","content":"A regional historical society that uses their knowledge of their territories past to dig up bans and banes for local spirits. The uratha at the core are made up of iron masters, storm lords and bone shadows and mostly come from wealthy backgrounds, either old money families from the region or executives from powerful companies with strong historical ties and cultural significance to the region","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T21:43:58-07:00","id":1068546,"title":"","content":"Debt collectors - don't mess with the repo-wolves.<br /> <br /> Burglers.<br /> <br /> Real estate agents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T22:05:01-07:00","id":1068549,"title":"","content":"The pack in our chronicle were all 'orphans', new wolves with no one else to turn to so they supported each other.<br /> \u200bOne had the effect of amnesia to represent that she was literally orphaned at such a young age she didn't know who her family was. Her parentage fueled the first arc of the chronicle.<br /> Another had family, at least up to the moment the Ivory Claws wiped them out. I don't think I have to explain how this one was played out.<br /> \u200bThe third still had a family, an extensive one made up of wolves and wolf blooded. She left them because she refused to accept the plans they had for her. The family was okay with existing in the background at first, after all they were confident she would come home eventually. Even after they realized she was never coming home they were okay with lending much needed assistance, in exchange for the child of a father of their choosing (this was 1ed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T23:26:39-07:00","id":1068558,"title":"","content":"I think I should mark that we need Pack concept AND typical Sacred Hunt of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-27-2017, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T08:44:59-07:00","id":1068690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066711-2e-pack-concepts?p=1068558#post1068558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I should mark that we need Pack concept AND typical Sacred Hunt of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do we? The pack concepts that we put up can be easily put between any and all tribe combinations - and personalities. The Sacred Hunt should be something your gaming table comes up with on your own so the flavors of the PC themselves gets represented.<br /> <br /> Not to mention everyone has a different OOC idea of how they'll have a Sacred Hunt play out per concept.<br /> <br /> I could see the merits in having a thread with examples of a Sacred Hunt (or other rituals) but to combine it with pack concepts feels off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 03-27-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T08:49:54-07:00","id":1068693,"title":"","content":"A thread with many examples of a 'Sacred Hunt', including the rituals the pack uses to start them, would be awesome. I wonder if someone has already made one? *Goes Digging*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:44:47-07:00","id":1076966,"title":"","content":"Made a pack for a vampire crossover. Half crazed ghost wolf Holly-Runs-With-Rats and a coterie of Nosferatu who basically became a sewer patrol due to the cities Beshilu threat. The treated themselves as doctors cutting the tumors from the city's body. &quot;Tumors need precision tools&quot; Johhny One Nut said &quot;but while most doctors use scalpels this tumor is much bigger and has legs, a tail, and a pipe wrench. Nurse we need to employ a larger tool&quot; Johhny then revved a chainsaw and threw himself into the coming onslaught. With celerity, vigor, and resilience he fought off the small horde. Holly on the other hand was dressed in a ww2 nurse outfit using her a fetish weapon to electrify the Beshilu. A weaponized shock treatment machine with a surge spirit inside it. The ending of that game was pure insanity and I loved it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T08:01:31-07:00","id":1076973,"title":"","content":"Also had an idea for a political pack, a group of anti-authoritarians trying to save human society from the beasts that pull the strings behind the scenes. Drawing on libertarian ideals as well as those of Hunter S. Thompson they are trying to save the American people from the corruption of the left and right for the benefit of the secret masters. Individualists who think they can protect the innocent. Could easily make up some interesting conceptual spirits for this pack to face off against.<br /> &quot;The mind of America is seized by a fatal dry rot - and it's only a question of time before all that the mind controls will run amuck in a frenzy of stupid, impotent fear&quot;- Hunter S Thompson","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T15:02:06-07:00","id":1079526,"title":"","content":"I think about 2-3 NPC pack I need for my Sweden Uppsala modern setting. I was going by using two Tribes per pack - to have variety of Uratha in region - but I seem to have problem with hammering in-game working concepts. My PCs pack sounds to be connected to gangs and criminal underworld in profile. I was thinking about those combinations:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Variant 1</b></span><ul><li><b>Pack 1</b> - Blood Talon + Bone Shadows - 'Traditionalist' - I do not know on what base pack here. Thought about maybe police force? But Bone Shadows do not seems to jive with idea.</li> <li><b>Pack 2</b> - Iron Masters + Storm Lords - 'Neo-pagans' - Pack connected to local univeristy and all 'neo-pagan' movement in it.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Variant 2</span></b><ul><li><b>Pack 3</b> - Blood Talon + Iron Masters - Police force pack, watching over humans and local Uratha. Works as 'good cop, bad cop'. Can see interesting interactions if PCs will be connected to criminals here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li><b>Pack 4</b> - Bones Shadows + Storm Lords - Neo-pagans from university, very serious about Nordic religion revival, and looking over Ridden and spirits.</li> </ul><br /> Writing this, it sounds to me that Variant 2 is general better packs spread and ideas...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T07:45:35-08:00","id":1160211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066711-2e-pack-concepts?p=1067940#post1067940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A dysfunctional family, whose mysterious matriarch lives at the edge of a tiny little Deep South town. The blood of the wolf runs strong, and any scions who show it are...brought home, whether they like it or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nercoing to add: A wealthy Downton Abby type landed family and their staff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T11:05:28-08:00","id":1160251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066711-2e-pack-concepts#post1066711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Clinic, health</div> </div> </div> </div>I just thought of doing a Werewolf chronicle based on Kamen Rider Ex-Aid...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T11:15:40-08:00","id":1160254,"title":"","content":"The Pack has a pack that's based around an elite hospital in, I think, Mexico. Where everyone in the staff, doctors down to janitors, are members of the pack in some form or another.<br /> <br /> Comedy troupe.<br /> <br /> Been playing Metal Gear Solid: the Phantom Pain, which is a very werewolf-like game. In that vein you have private military contractors, basically mercenary units (complete with administration and support infrastructure for those who are not combat-oriented).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-18-2017, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}